WEBVTT

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:46.370
Are you still messing with that, Nishi?

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.170
Y-Yes, almost done...

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.670
Make it quick. We don't have much time.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.260
R-Right...

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:00.640
S-Sorry to keep you.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.750
Wh-What's the matter, old man?

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.850
Is Joe asleep?

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:10.670
Yeah...

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:15.260
He hasn't eaten a thing all day, either.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:23.450
He just had an awful fight, after all.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:26.700
It's probably best he rest without thinking about anything.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.410
You got that right.{ts sign after this?}

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:32.510
Hey, old man, don't you think people die way too easily?

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:34.560
I know his weight loss wasn't normal...

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:37.030
But I still can't believe it.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.160
Don't you think it's just crazy?

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:45.070
Nishi, look at how grand his funeral is.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.870
Rikiishi's really dead, isn't he?

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.840
If it isn't Tange-san.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:27.740
Thank you.

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.490
Don't mention it.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:34.990
Joe was supposed to come with me, but the doctor said no.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.920
He's been resting ever since.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.960
Please excuse him.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:47.340
I will bring him to see you once he wakes up.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.700
Now, allow me to pay my respects.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.170
Rikiishi-kun...

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:30.690
The flower that you made blossom in the ring

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:35.150
was truly, truly beautiful.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.900
Hey, isn't Yabuki Joe coming?

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:55.450
Why hasn't the guy that drove Rikiishi to death shown himself?

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.460
Apparently the doctor told him to stay in bed.

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:01.680
I guess he did get knocked down a lot...

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:04.180
He must've taken quite a bit of damage,

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:06.820
but that shouldn't be a reason for him not to come!

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:08.430
Well, you have a point...

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.830
I think he should show himself, even if it's a strain on his system.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:12.990
That's just common courtesy.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.430
You're right.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:17.380
Well, why don't we go check in on him?

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:18.960
Yeah! Let's do that!

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:27.440
Yabuki-kun! Yabuki-kun!

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.070
You think he's sleeping?

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:32.650
No matter.

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:35.080
Why don't we go inside?

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.690
Could he be sleeping up here?

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:42.540
What should we do?

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.030
You go and see him.

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:45.590
Are you sure that's all right?

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:49.590
It'll be fine! If he's asleep, at least get a photo!

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.380
Where could he be?

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:07.130
You think he might have been hospitalized?

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:08.070
Maybe.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.480
Hey! Come on!

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:11.570
Get him!

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:12.710
Isn't that Yabuki?

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:14.580
It is! What's he up to here?

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:18.080
Now, stare each other down...

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:24.830
Now, this is getting interesting!

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:26.590
It's 3-3, and this is the tiebreaker!

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:29.050
Stare each other down...

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.550
Keep staring! Don't start yet!

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:40.560
Hey, sumo is boring! Let's play something else!

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.560
Just wait! This is getting good!

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:48.420
No way! You only play boy games like sword-fighting or sumo!

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:50.570
I always get left out!

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.340
Shut up!

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:53.570
Pipe down!

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:57.680
Well, you're pretty strong, Sachi! You should give it a try!

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:59.080
How does the name "Sachinohana" sound?

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.200
You gotta be kidding me! You little-!{retime to include "konoyaro" at the end}

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:06.040
I'm a girl! You expect me to play your barbaric boy games?

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:08.340
Gimme a break...

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:11.380
Yowch! That's not fair, Kinoko!

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.380
Why, you little...

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:18.200
No, Kinoko! I haven't given the signal yet!

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:21.210
You can't get up until I say so!

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:22.800
That's what I call a head start!

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.850
Dammit! I won't go easy on you now!

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:27.360
All right, keep staring... Not yet...

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:29.690
Give it your all...

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:30.360
And you're in!{tlc: is this like "ready set go"}

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:33.140
You're in! You're in!

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:35.080
<i>It's still on! It's still on!</i>

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:38.190
Well, he's pretty happy-go-lucky...

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:39.870
This is a real surprise.

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:44.020
To think, he was playing with children instead of going to the funeral...

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:47.430
Hey, Kinoko! You're on the edge!

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:51.880
And the fight's over!

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:54.260
Kinokodake {pun on Takeshi Futagodake}wins with a last-minute reversal!

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:56.320
How'd you like that?

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:00.760
No, I won fair and square!
 Kinoko's legs went out before I did!

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:04.270
Yeah, it did look like Kinoko's legs were out...

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:08.860
Due to a complaint from the observers, this match will have to be redone!

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:12.200
That's total crap! When did my legs go out?

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:14.030
They did! They did! They sure did!

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:17.940
Stop lying! They didn't! I saw!

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:19.880
How can you wrestle looking at your legs?

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:22.940
Stop the sumo! Stop it! It's stupid! It's stupid!

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:24.380
Right, right.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:26.370
This time, everyone come at me together!

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:28.380
Okay...

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.640
All right...

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:31.840
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!{joe has a line here? or is it just a sound effect}

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:36.880
You're strong, you're strong! You're all strong!

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:44.450
Well, I guess it's hard for the guy who killed him to show his face at the funeral.

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:51.860
But he could at least light a stick of incense or shed a tear for him!

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.860
Should I take a picture of him playing with the kids?

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:01.870
Forget it. I couldn't write this article, out of respect for Shiraki Gym.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:05.830
That Yabuki's heart is a wasteland where not even grass or moss grows!

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:08.290
He's suffered his first loss by KO,

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:10.780
but his opponent died.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:14.840
Don't you think a guy like that would be satisfied by that outcome?

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:46.270
I'll have supper ready soon!

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:49.500
You and the kids will have to wait, dear.

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:52.430
We're not eating grass and mud!

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:55.500
What do girls find fun about this?

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:58.510
It's no fun doing what <i>she</i> wants.

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:01.540
Shut up! I waited for you guys!

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:03.510
Now you have to play with me!

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:08.430
Here, Papa-san! Have this! It's quite good!{retimed}

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:19.600
Joe?

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:22.980
Bro Joe? Why don't we have some real food?

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:26.920
There should be some left in your kitchen, right, Bro Joe?

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:28.620
Come on, Bro Joe!

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:29.560
Rikiishi...

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:49.960
I-I have to go home...

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:55.780
Me too...

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:58.750
Mom's gonna yell at me if I'm late for dinner...

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:03.140
I suppose I'll go back home...

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:30.290
Joe...

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:49.150
What's that, old man?

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:52.390
That sound...

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:55.230
It sounds like someone hitting a sandbag!

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.140
That damn Joe!

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:04.730
It's pitch black in here! Nishi, the lights!

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:06.270
Joe!

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.660
Joe, what are you doing?

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:15.660
You're in no condition to train!

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:19.730
The doctor was very clear that you need to rest!

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:21.090
Here.

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:27.580
How was Rikiishi's funeral?

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:34.810
It was grand. There were a lot of big-shots there.

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:44.960
Yoko...

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:46.600
Was she crying?

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:54.070
No, it looked like she was in control of her feelings.

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:55.610
She was calm and composed.

00:16:58.420 --> 00:17:01.120
It was an accident. There wasn't a thing anyone could've done.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.440
It's too stuffy in here for this sweat I've worked up!

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:07.140
I'm gonna go take a walk.

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:13.090
J-Joe!

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:20.670
Joe!

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:47.580
O-Old man! Look at that!

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:07.110
That son of a bitch...

00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:09.450
He hit it bare-handed...

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:15.900
I-I can't believe that Joe hit it until he started bleeding...

00:19:04.900 --> 00:19:05.920
Rikiishi...

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:13.000
Rikiishi!

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:32.870
Rikiishi...

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:41.940
I guess I can't tell you not to think about it...

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:44.630
Just don't overthink it.

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:49.140
Give me your hands.

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:58.310
Now, Joe, there's no need to obsess over it.

00:20:58.830 --> 00:21:03.730
This is a tragedy that's common for boxers, especially ones like you.

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:09.890
Countless fighters in Japan and overseas have been through the exact same thing.

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:13.760
And there are some who are ruined by the shock.

00:21:13.760 --> 00:21:18.400
But there are many more fighters who overcome it.

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:24.200
I think I'm gonna be ruined.

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:27.310
Joe...

00:21:32.110 --> 00:21:35.900
Seeing Rikiishi's dead face did something to my head.

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:40.310
Rikiishi's dead and gone from this world.{original tl: "dead and no longer in this world"}

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:44.640
Whenever I think that, my head feels empty.

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:49.410
Not just my head. My stomach, my heart, my hands and feet...

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:53.730
I feel like there's a huge hole in me, and the wind's blowing through it.

00:21:56.050 --> 00:21:57.200
What am I supposed to do?

00:21:57.700 --> 00:21:59.720
I don't know.

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:09.870
Hey...

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:12.170
Do you mind leaving me alone?

00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:14.560
I want to be alone.

00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:21.620
I said leave me alone!

00:22:21.620 --> 00:22:24.220
Don't you get it, you assholes?

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:49.920
Look. Everyone's worried about you.

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:00.730
Out of my way!

00:23:02.710 --> 00:23:12.410
Joe!

00:23:12.820 --> 00:23:15.950
Joe! Where are you going?

00:23:16.490 --> 00:23:18.550
Joe!

00:23:19.260 --> 00:23:21.050
Joe!

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:45.480
Yuke kouya wo

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:45.480
Go to the wilderness!

00:23:46.670 --> 00:23:49.420
Oira boxer

00:23:46.670 --> 00:23:49.420
I am a boxer.

00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:57.180
Yuuhi ga giragira otoko no yume wa

00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:57.180
The evening sun glitters upon the dreams of men!

00:23:58.890 --> 00:24:02.850
Minna wa kono ore wo nasakemuyo to iu

00:23:58.890 --> 00:24:02.850
Everyone says that I am merciless.

00:24:02.850 --> 00:24:04.900
Tsuki ni hoete hitori

00:24:02.850 --> 00:24:04.900
Howling at the moon alone.

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:11.280
Oyanashi yadonashi no na mo nai boxer wa

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:11.280
A parentless, homeless, nameless boxer

00:24:11.280 --> 00:24:14.430
Kusari wo kamikitta Yeah Yeah!

00:24:11.280 --> 00:24:14.430
has bitten off his chains! Yeah, yeah!

00:24:15.830 --> 00:24:18.740
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:15.830 --> 00:24:18.740
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:19.950 --> 00:24:22.460
Oira boxer

00:24:19.950 --> 00:24:22.460
I am a boxer.

00:24:23.580 --> 00:24:30.720
Asahi ga noboru yo otoko no mune ni {removed the Woo, but otherwise japanese is unchanged - Reed}

00:24:23.580 --> 00:24:30.720
The morning sun rises upon the hearts of men!

00:24:36.570 --> 00:24:37.770
The snow falls.

00:24:38.400 --> 00:24:41.390
Amidst the falling white snow,

00:24:41.390 --> 00:24:44.030
a miserable Joe runs away.

00:24:45.420 --> 00:24:48.960
He aimlessly wanders the city of falling snow.

00:24:49.960 --> 00:24:53.970
But Joe's heart, filled with loneliness,

00:24:54.440 --> 00:24:56.970
hears the song of Rikiishi.

00:24:57.280 --> 00:24:59.970
The song of the heart of Rikiishi, who passed away so fleetingly!

00:25:01.530 --> 00:25:06.580
Now, as Joe embraces Rikiishi's shadow and sheds tears,

00:25:06.580 --> 00:25:07.970
which way is tomorrow!?{this looks like the preview and the ED has been switched in the encode}
